<section id="intro">
<h1>Affiliate Marketing vs MLM: What's the Difference?</h1>

<p><strong>Most beginners cannot tell the difference.</strong> And that is understandable — because multi-level marketing (MLM) companies have spent years deliberately adopting the language of affiliate marketing to appear legitimate. "Join our affiliate program," their pitch says. "Earn commissions on every level." The terminology overlap is not accidental.</p>

<p>But affiliate marketing and MLM are fundamentally different business models. The difference is not cosmetic — it is structural, legal, and practical. Getting it wrong can cost you time, money, and relationships. Getting it right can set you on a path to genuine online income.</p>

<p>This guide breaks down every difference that matters, based on FTC regulatory guidance, income disclosure data, and real community experiences. No hype, no recruitment pitch — just the facts you need to make an informed decision.</p>
</section>

<GoldMasterQuote />

<section id="core-difference">
<h2>The Core Difference: Single-Level vs Multi-Level Compensation</h2>

<p>Everything else flows from this one structural choice:</p>

<div class="table-scroll">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Dimension</th>
      <th>Affiliate Marketing</th>
      <th>Multi-Level Marketing</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Compensation levels</strong></td>
      <td>One level — you earn on your direct sales only</td>
      <td>Multiple levels — you earn on personal sales plus a percentage of sales by everyone you recruit (and their recruits)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Primary income driver</strong></td>
      <td>Traffic generation and conversion skills</td>
      <td>Recruitment and team management</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Do you need to recruit?</strong></td>
      <td>No — you can earn a full-time income without recruiting a single person</td>
      <td>Yes — meaningful income requires building and maintaining a downline</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p>This single difference — one level vs many levels — creates two completely different businesses. One rewards your ability to drive traffic and convert readers. The other rewards your ability to recruit and manage people.</p>
</section>

